<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="2" dur="3.12">Mr. President,</text><text start="3.04" dur="4.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; hello everybody. So,</text><text start="5.12" dur="6.24">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; we had a tremendous day in Texas. We had</text><text start="7.68" dur="5.76">two big rallies. They were packed. They</text><text start="11.36" dur="3.68">had people watching outside the screens.</text><text start="13.44" dur="4.32">We put up the big screens, the</text><text start="15.04" dur="5.44">jumbotrons or whatever they call, but</text><text start="17.76" dur="5.04">they were big packed rallies and people</text><text start="20.48" dur="4.32">haven&amp;#39;t really seen anything like it.</text><text start="22.8" dur="4.239">And it&amp;#39;s very exciting. I think we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="24.8" dur="3.92">made a big impact. We&amp;#39;ll see what</text><text start="27.039" dur="4.24">happens on Tuesday. But I think we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="28.72" dur="4.16">made a big impact. It&amp;#39;s very exciting</text><text start="31.279" dur="4.081">what&amp;#39;s going on. I&amp;#39;m going to be going</text><text start="32.88" dur="5.199">to Ohio. I&amp;#39;ll be going to South</text><text start="35.36" dur="7.12">Carolina. She&amp;#39;s doing well. She&amp;#39;s at a</text><text start="38.079" dur="8.081">poll where she&amp;#39;s up. And it&amp;#39;s Darlene.</text><text start="42.48" dur="5.599">And uh I think in Ohio they are up too.</text><text start="46.16" dur="5.28">So we&amp;#39;re doing very well. We&amp;#39;re having a</text><text start="48.079" dur="5.681">very big impact. See you from Lavio</text><text start="51.44" dur="4.48">Baltimore coming to the United States.</text><text start="53.76" dur="5.439">What is that about? Well, I would</text><text start="55.92" dur="6.319">approve. I think they&amp;#39;re fine people.</text><text start="59.199" dur="5.04">The election was very strange</text><text start="62.239" dur="3.601">and I thought it was terrible. It&amp;#39;s</text><text start="64.239" dur="4.081">gotten bad reviews. You look at what</text><text start="65.84" dur="4.24">happened to their market. Would I</text><text start="68.32" dur="4.24">approve of it? Yeah, I would approve it.</text><text start="70.08" dur="4.64">I would think it would be okay with me.</text><text start="72.56" dur="4.239">I think it&amp;#39;s so terrible to see it. I</text><text start="74.72" dur="4.24">didn&amp;#39;t take sides. You know, I know him</text><text start="76.799" dur="5.201">both. I know</text><text start="78.96" dur="5.44">Lula. I know Lavio a little bit. I know</text><text start="82" dur="5.36">the father very well. The father was</text><text start="84.4" dur="4.88">treated really badly, I thought. Uh, but</text><text start="87.36" dur="3.52">I wasn&amp;#39;t involved. That&amp;#39;s Brazil. It&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="89.28" dur="3.92">different country. I do get involved in</text><text start="90.88" dur="5.279">some. I was involved in Colombia. I</text><text start="93.2" dur="5.2">endorsed Elte and he won. He was in 10th</text><text start="96.159" dur="5.521">place and he won and he&amp;#39;s turning out to</text><text start="98.4" dur="4.96">be a very strong, very good president.</text><text start="101.68" dur="3.759">Uh, as you know, in Argentina, I</text><text start="103.36" dur="3.439">endorsed in numerous countries I</text><text start="105.439" dur="4.161">endorsed. They always won. I didn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="106.799" dur="5.6">endorse in Brazil. I thought I&amp;#39;d stay</text><text start="109.6" dur="4.799">out of that one. And I thought the uh</text><text start="112.399" dur="4.161">end result, you know, it&amp;#39;s fine the end</text><text start="114.399" dur="3.201">result, but the way they got to the end</text><text start="116.56" dur="3.76">result was terrible.</text><text start="117.6" dur="5.36">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Where is he in Miami or I</text><text start="120.32" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I heard he was in Argentina. I don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="122.96" dur="2.4">know where he is. I mean, I heard he was</text><text start="124.32" dur="2.32">in Argentina.</text><text start="125.36" dur="3.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; The United States,</text><text start="126.64" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; but I I don&amp;#39;t I don&amp;#39;t know. I heard he</text><text start="129.2" dur="3.759">was in Argentina,</text><text start="131.12" dur="4.479">but yeah, I would certainly approve of</text><text start="132.959" dur="6.721">him being here.</text><text start="135.599" dur="6.64">people out of Israel right now that</text><text start="139.68" dur="4">coalition is losing peace and unlikely</text><text start="142.239" dur="3.601">that he would continue.</text><text start="143.68" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, that&amp;#39;s not what I heard. I heard</text><text start="145.84" dur="5.039">that I heard the opposite. I actually</text><text start="148.64" dur="4.959">heard that the poll numbers were wrong.</text><text start="150.879" dur="4.401">They had exit polls that I&amp;#39;m hearing</text><text start="153.599" dur="5.681">that he did very well. It&amp;#39;s, you know,</text><text start="155.28" dur="5.599">it&amp;#39;s pretty close, which was very well.</text><text start="159.28" dur="3.92">I think when the endorsement went out,</text><text start="160.879" dur="3.841">it it helped him a lot. But I actually</text><text start="163.2" dur="4.16">heard he did pretty well. It might be</text><text start="164.72" dur="4.64">winning or tied. The tie is sort of</text><text start="167.36" dur="5.84">considered a win in that case because</text><text start="169.36" dur="5.92">it&amp;#39;s a big chess match. And but I I</text><text start="173.2" dur="4.56">heard he&amp;#39;s doing pretty well. It&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="175.28" dur="4.959">little bit early. No, I haven&amp;#39;t. It&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="177.76" dur="5.6">little bit early yet. But I&amp;#39;m hearing</text><text start="180.239" dur="5.28">that in Israel that he I mean the top</text><text start="183.36" dur="4.32">people are saying, &amp;quot;Wow, he did a lot</text><text start="185.519" dur="6">better than people thought.&amp;quot; Sort of</text><text start="187.68" dur="7.8">like maybe a stalemate or a win. But</text><text start="191.519" dur="3.961">we&amp;#39;ll find out pretty soon.</text><text start="201.36" dur="5.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, uh, Ambassador Kushner, you</text><text start="203.68" dur="6.479">talking France. He&amp;#39;s a great guy. He&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="206.8" dur="6.32">rich man and he took over the French</text><text start="210.159" dur="4.881">embassy and he spends a lot of his time</text><text start="213.12" dur="4">making it beautiful. Was in rough shape.</text><text start="215.04" dur="4.32">beautiful building, but you know, it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="217.12" dur="4.479">been lived in for</text><text start="219.36" dur="5.28">a hundred years by various ambassadors</text><text start="221.599" dur="5.121">and nobody does anything. He&amp;#39;s somebody</text><text start="224.64" dur="4.8">like me, I guess. He likes to fix things</text><text start="226.72" dur="5.439">up and uh he&amp;#39;s done an incredible job.</text><text start="229.44" dur="5.359">He&amp;#39;s painstakingly brought it back to</text><text start="232.159" dur="5.44">life. It&amp;#39;s a beautiful, beautiful place,</text><text start="234.799" dur="6.321">beautiful embassy, beautiful home. Uh,</text><text start="237.599" dur="5.28">and we talked about France and obviously</text><text start="241.12" dur="4">it would be a predominant. He was</text><text start="242.879" dur="4.801">showing me what he did, but then we</text><text start="245.12" dur="4.64">talked about France and it&amp;#39;s an</text><text start="247.68" dur="3.68">immigration problem. I mean, it&amp;#39;s not a</text><text start="249.76" dur="3.759">school problem. It&amp;#39;s an immigration</text><text start="251.36" dur="4.239">problem. It&amp;#39;s a very sad thing to watch.</text><text start="253.519" dur="3.921">I&amp;#39;ve been saying that to President</text><text start="255.599" dur="4.081">Mcronone for a long time, who I like a</text><text start="257.44" dur="3.68">lot, by the way. But I said, you&amp;#39;re</text><text start="259.68" dur="3.76">going to end up losing your country if</text><text start="261.12" dur="5.2">you don&amp;#39;t do something. But it&amp;#39;s an</text><text start="263.44" dur="5.199">immigration. You have people that hate</text><text start="266.32" dur="5.76">France. They hate the buildings, hate</text><text start="268.639" dur="5.84">the art, hate the they hate the people.</text><text start="272.08" dur="3.76">And they&amp;#39;re in there and</text><text start="274.479" dur="3.841">you&amp;#39;d have to get them out. Something</text><text start="275.84" dur="4.799">has to happen and they better do</text><text start="278.32" dur="4.64">something. I&amp;#39;ve been saying it for 10</text><text start="280.639" dur="6.321">years to the president. I&amp;#39;ve known him</text><text start="282.96" dur="5.92">for a long time and it&amp;#39;s</text><text start="286.96" dur="6.959">I think what&amp;#39;s happened in France and</text><text start="288.88" dur="6.96">other countries in Europe is very sad.</text><text start="293.919" dur="3.681">with Steve Whit on the plane with you</text><text start="295.84" dur="3.68">today. Can you tell us what you</text><text start="297.6" dur="2.8">discussed? Is it related to Iran or</text><text start="299.52" dur="2.72">Russia?</text><text start="300.4" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; We talked about Iran, talked about</text><text start="302.24" dur="5.76">Russia and I think with Russia, we&amp;#39;re</text><text start="304.88" dur="4.64">making a lot of progress with Russia</text><text start="308" dur="3.199">Ukraine.</text><text start="309.52" dur="3.44">There&amp;#39;ll be a meeting set up very soon.</text><text start="311.199" dur="5.521">And I think a lot of progress is being</text><text start="312.96" dur="6.16">made to stop with President Putin and</text><text start="316.72" dur="4.479">President Zullinski.</text><text start="319.12" dur="4.56">And I think a lot of progress is made. I</text><text start="321.199" dur="4.161">think uh with Iran, we&amp;#39;re in a very good</text><text start="323.68" dur="3.519">position.</text><text start="325.36" dur="4.8">It&amp;#39;s a question when do I want to end</text><text start="327.199" dur="6.481">it. Simply a question of when do I want</text><text start="330.16" dur="4.879">to end it and uh they want I they want</text><text start="333.68" dur="3.519">to make a deal, but they&amp;#39;ve wanted to</text><text start="335.039" dur="4.241">make a deal, but they like tapping it</text><text start="337.199" dur="3.84">along. Maybe they&amp;#39;re waiting for the</text><text start="339.28" dur="3.919">election or something, but that&amp;#39;s not</text><text start="341.039" dur="4.961">going to help them. The election&amp;#39;s not</text><text start="343.199" dur="4.961">going to help them. But I I think we&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="346" dur="4.72">uh look, we&amp;#39;ve decimated their military.</text><text start="348.16" dur="5.12">We&amp;#39;ve decimated their finances. They</text><text start="350.72" dur="5.919">have no money. They have inflation, the</text><text start="353.28" dur="5.919">highest in the world, 301% as of a</text><text start="356.639" dur="4.241">couple of days ago, but we&amp;#39;ll see what</text><text start="359.199" dur="3.521">happens. We&amp;#39;re in good position</text><text start="360.88" dur="3.84">regardless.</text><text start="362.72" dur="3.759">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Strikes against Iran after the election.</text><text start="364.72" dur="4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I can&amp;#39;t tell you that. I mean, I can&amp;#39;t</text><text start="366.479" dur="3.921">tell you that certainly, but</text><text start="368.72" dur="4.96">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; anything&amp;#39;s possible, but I can&amp;#39;t tell</text><text start="370.4" dur="6.48">you. vice president said recently that</text><text start="373.68" dur="6.4">he expects your support if he runs for</text><text start="376.88" dur="4.96">president. Uh would you endorse him?</text><text start="380.08" dur="3.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, no, he hasn&amp;#39;t even talked to me</text><text start="381.84" dur="4.4">about that and it&amp;#39;s too early to think</text><text start="384" dur="4.639">about it. But I can tell you I like him</text><text start="386.24" dur="3.679">a lot. He&amp;#39;s a very capable guy. He&amp;#39;s</text><text start="388.639" dur="4.56">doing a good job. He&amp;#39;s out there</text><text start="389.919" dur="7.441">rallying also and I do like him a lot</text><text start="393.199" dur="6.801">and I like a lot of people. You saw the</text><text start="397.36" dur="5.36">hand that Marco got tonight. Marco Rubio</text><text start="400" dur="4.639">got a big hand and they like him. They</text><text start="402.72" dur="4.4">like my people. We have a a great group</text><text start="404.639" dur="5.28">of people. Very talented. It&amp;#39;s a</text><text start="407.12" dur="4.32">tremendous cabinet. I think maybe the</text><text start="409.919" dur="3.201">best ever.</text><text start="411.44" dur="3.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; When would you meet with Putin and</text><text start="413.12" dur="5.6">Zelinski? When when are you thinking</text><text start="415.28" dur="4.8">about it soon, you know,</text><text start="418.72" dur="2.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; and I would say it would be a meeting.</text><text start="420.08" dur="3.119">They&amp;#39;d like to have a meeting. So, we&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="421.44" dur="3.84">see. We&amp;#39;ll probably make it could be</text><text start="423.199" dur="4.4">done not necessarily through a meeting</text><text start="425.28" dur="4.08">otherwise too but I would say it&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="427.599" dur="4.72">happen over the next not too long a</text><text start="429.36" dur="4.88">period.</text><text start="432.319" dur="3.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; That does not include Zilinski when you</text><text start="434.24" dur="3.679">go to Asia.</text><text start="435.759" dur="4.241">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I would if it didn&amp;#39;t include</text><text start="437.919" dur="5.12">Ukraine. You know, Russia is a big</text><text start="440" dur="5.84">country. uh we&amp;#39;re meeting with uh</text><text start="443.039" dur="7.041">scheduled already with President Xi of</text><text start="445.84" dur="6.079">China and we have a meeting on nuclear</text><text start="450.08" dur="3.92">disarmament which is a very great</text><text start="451.919" dur="4.801">meeting as far as I&amp;#39;m concerned maybe</text><text start="454" dur="4.72">the single most important meeting so we</text><text start="456.72" dur="5.599">do have we talk about the</text><text start="458.72" dur="5.919">denuclearization of uh the various</text><text start="462.319" dur="5.121">countries so certainly Russia would fit</text><text start="464.639" dur="5.601">into we have the most nuclear weapons</text><text start="467.44" dur="5.28">Russia second pretty close pretty close</text><text start="470.24" dur="5.28">behind behind and China&amp;#39;s much further</text><text start="472.72" dur="6.479">behind, but they&amp;#39;ll catch us within 5</text><text start="475.52" dur="5.44">years and it all doesn&amp;#39;t make sense. So,</text><text start="479.199" dur="3.12">we talk about that. We actually talk</text><text start="480.96" dur="3.28">about it a lot.</text><text start="482.319" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I guess they don&amp;#39;t have a meeting on</text><text start="484.24" dur="5.359">nuclear disarmament with President Xi</text><text start="486.879" dur="7.521">and President Putin. we would have one</text><text start="489.599" dur="9.6">of the topics but the denuclearization</text><text start="494.4" dur="8.479">I mean when you look at 17800</text><text start="499.199" dur="8.241">of these unbelievably deadly</text><text start="502.879" dur="7.44">missiles it&amp;#39;s uh very dangerous stuff</text><text start="507.44" dur="5.76">very very dangerous stuff if something</text><text start="510.319" dur="5.121">could be done in that regard it would be</text><text start="513.2" dur="4.16">great it&amp;#39;s not an easy thing to do</text><text start="515.44" dur="3.92">because nobody wants to sort of just say</text><text start="517.36" dur="4.88">Well, because you do have other</text><text start="519.36" dur="5.2">countries having much lesser numbers,</text><text start="522.24" dur="4.24">but they also have nuclear weapons. So,</text><text start="524.56" dur="4.92">it gets to be difficult. Thank you very</text><text start="526.48" dur="3">much.</text></transcript>